<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- W^X JIT for Android JS engines run natively (cohtml's V8 renders MCPE's
         Ore-UI menu). allow-jit permits MAP_JIT + pthread_jit_write_protect;
         allow-unsigned-executable-memory permits mprotect(RX) on freshly-written
         RW pages (the W^X code-modification path). Persistent RWX is still blocked
         under ad-hoc signing; the mprotect shim translates a guest RWX request to
         a transient RW write phase (see __macapk_arm64_mprotect). -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- v1.0.1017: needed once the bundle is signed with a Developer ID rather
         than ad-hoc. Library validation would otherwise refuse the runtime's
         dlopen of ANGLE / MoltenVK / libjvm, which are signed by other teams or
         not at all. Ad hoc signing does not enforce it, which is why the dev
         path never needed this key and why its absence here stayed invisible
         until a release build was contemplated.
         It arrived here because launcher/MacApk.entitlements (the file
         scripts/build_dist.sh used to sign with) carried THIS key but not
         custom-x18-abi-toggle, device.camera or device.audio-input, while this
         file carried those three but not this one. Two files, drifted in BOTH
         directions, and a forced codesign with an entitlements argument
         REPLACES the whole blob rather than merging it. There is now ONE file;
         do not reintroduce a second.
         NOTE: no double hyphen may appear anywhere in this comment. It closes
         the XML comment early, plutil accepts it anyway, and AMFI then rejects
         the plist at codesign time with a syntax error that names neither the
         file nor the cause. That is exactly how this edit failed once. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- Durable x18 preservation (macOS 26.4+). This entitlement makes XNU
         honor a SELF-set TPIDR_EL0 bit 48 (MACHDEP_TPIDR_FLAG_PRESERVE_X18)
         across context switches, so x18 survives EL0 exception returns for
         each thread that OR-s the bit in. Guest Android arm64 code (Unity,
         cocos2d-x, hand-asm FMOD) uses x18 as a general-purpose register,
         which macOS otherwise clobbers. Note: .security. (NOT .private.) so
         it is honored for ad-hoc third-party binaries under SIP; same
         com.apple.security.* family as allow-jit above. As of v1.0.1018 this
         is the ONLY x18 mechanism: the deprecated sdk-below-13
         LC_BUILD_VERSION gate and its MACAPK_X18_SDK_GATE option were
         deleted, so there is no fallback below macOS 26.4. See
         docs/x18-custom-abi-toggle-entitlement_2026-07-14.md. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.custom-x18-abi-toggle</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- v1.0.940: real microphone and camera capture (audio_input.mm /
         camera_capture.mm). These are HARDENED RUNTIME "Resource Access" keys,
         NOT App Sandbox keys: the sandbox spellings are the different
         com.apple.security.device.microphone / .camera, and we are not
         sandboxed. This binary is signed by build.sh with codesign's
         hardened-runtime option, so these are the ones TCC consults.
         The bundle's Info.plist usage strings (launcher/Info.plist:113) are the
         other half and were already present. One half without the other can
         yield a SILENT denial rather than a prompt, which is the failure mode
         hardest to diagnose from the app side. If capture ever fails with no
         prompt, dump the signed entitlements with codesign and check both keys
         are present.

         WARNING TO THE NEXT EDITOR: do NOT write a double hyphen anywhere in
         this comment. XML forbids it inside a comment, and AMFI's parser
         enforces that where `plutil -lint` does not: it accepts the file, then
         codesign fails with "AMFIUnserializeXML: syntax error", make DELETES
         the linked binary, and the build stops. That is exactly how v1.0.940
         first broke, by spelling out a codesign flag here. The project's
         house style of writing a double hyphen in place of an em dash does not
         apply to XML. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- Mac Location Services for android.location (location_bridge.mm).
         The hardened runtime Resource Access key for CoreLocation; without it
         TCC refuses this binary location without ever showing the prompt,
         however complete the bundle usage string is. Same rule as the two
         keys above: one half without the other is a SILENT denial. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.location</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- Bluetooth for android.bluetooth (bluetooth_bridge.mm and
         bluetooth_peripheral_bridge.mm, opt-in via MACAPK_BLUETOOTH_HOST).
         The hardened runtime Resource Access key for CoreBluetooth; same rule
         as the keys above: the bundle usage string is only half of it, and
         one half without the other is a silent denial or a TCC kill, not a
         prompt. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.bluetooth</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
